module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.CoherentStackAlgebraicUnconditional
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.QuotFunctorAlgebraicFromExistence

/-!
# The Quot functor is an algebraic space (Stacks 09TU, first assertion)

Let `f : X ⟶ B` be a separated morphism of algebraic spaces of finite presentation and `F` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module.  Stacks 09TU says that `Quot_{F/X/B}` is an algebraic space.  The
proof: the 1-morphism `Quot_{F/X/B} ⟶ Coh_{X/B}` is representable by algebraic spaces, its fibre
over an object `(T, 𝒢)` being the open subspace of surjections of the relative Hom space
`Hom(F_T, 𝒢)` (Stacks 08K6, 09TP), and `Coh_{X/B}` is an algebraic stack (Stacks 09DS, from
Grothendieck's existence theorem 0CXB), so the stack `Quot_{F/X/B}` is algebraic (Stacks 05UM), and
a stack in setoids which is algebraic is an algebraic space (Stacks 04SZ).

## Main results

* `QuotSituation.isAlgebraicSpace_quotSitePresheafModel_of_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow`:
  every model of `Quot_{F/X/B}` in the universe of the site is an algebraic space, for `F`
  étale-locally generated by fewer than `μ` sections with `μ` below the cutoff of the site.

## Implementation notes

On a big fppf site, whose schemes are bounded in size by a cutoff `κ`, the first assertion of
Stacks 09TU fails for an arbitrary quasi-coherent `F`, for the reason the first assertion of Stacks
08K6 does; it is stated here for `F` étale-locally generated by fewer than `μ` sections for some
`μ < κ`, which every `F` of finite type is
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow_lt_cutoff_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09TU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09TU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09DS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09DS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08K6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08K6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CXB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CXB)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory

universe u

attribute [local implicit_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.toCoherentSituation

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S} (D : QuotSituation B S hS)

/-- **Stacks 09TU, the first assertion, for `F` with a bound on its local generators.**  Let
`f : X ⟶ B` be separated and of finite presentation and let `F` be étale-locally generated by
fewer than `μ` sections, `μ` below the cutoff of the site (for instance `F` of finite type).  Then
every model of `Quot_{F/X/B}` in the universe of the site is an algebraic space. -/
theorem isAlgebraicSpace_quotSitePresheafModel_of_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow
    (hsep : IsSeparated B S hS D.f.hom)
    (hF : ∃ μ < B.cutoff, IsEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow B S hS μ D.F)
    (M : QuotSitePresheafModel D) : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS M.presheaf :=
  M.isAlgebraicSpace_of_homRepresentations.{u, u + 1}
    (D.hasHomRepresentation_of_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow hF)
    (CoherentSituation.isAlgebraicStack_coherentCFG.{u, u + 1} D.toCoherentSituation hsep)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation

end
